    "Across all five runs, Web Content RSS increased between completed cycle 100 and 600 with the same shared fingerprint, 600 cycles, and measured 6.65?6.97 Hz rates. Disabling action snapshots did not remove the increase.",
    "The no_addons and neither variants still showed substantial Web Content RSS growth; no_addons had the largest 100-to-600 increase. Disabling default addons reduced sampled WebExtensions RSS, but did not prevent page-process growth.",
    "After 25 seconds of natural idle, baseline anon memory fell by about 852 MiB from its cycle-600 sample; no_addons retained most of its cycle-600 anon memory. The GC-contrast run had already released most observed anon memory during its 15-second natural settle; only about 32 MiB additional anon decrease was seen in the later sample window, which does not isolate a forced-GC effect.",
    "The Web Content process is the dominant growing per-process RSS series in these samples. The data do not identify the exact engine subsystem or prove a memory leak; file cache, anon cgroup accounting, and process RSS are distinct measurements.",
